{"tool_name":"deepcell","contents":["biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:deepcell"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"deepcell","home":"https://www.deepcell.org","summary":"Accurate cell tracking and lineage construction in live-cell imaging experiments with deep learning.\n\nHome \u2014 DeepCell 1.0.0 documentation.\n\nFree document hosting provided by Read the Docs","addition_date":"2020-01-09T18:27:38Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:38:22.175336Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:deepcell","documentation":[{"type":["FAQ"],"url":"https://www.deepcell.org/faq"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://www.deepcell.org/about"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://deepcell.readthedocs.io/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Image analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443"},{"term":"Image annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3553"}]}],"name":"DeepCell","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41592-020-01023-0","metadata":{"abstract":"Deep learning is transforming the analysis of biological images, but applying these models to large datasets remains challenging. Here we describe the DeepCell Kiosk, cloud-native software that dynamically scales deep learning workflows to accommodate large imaging datasets. To demonstrate the scalability and affordability of this software, we identified cell nuclei in 106 1-megapixel images in ~5.5 h for ~US$250, with a cost below US$100 achievable depending on cluster configuration. The DeepCell Kiosk can be downloaded at https://github.com/vanvalenlab/kiosk-console; a persistent deployment is available at https://deepcell.org/.","authors":[{"name":"Bannon D."},{"name":"Borba E."},{"name":"Chang B."},{"name":"Graf W."},{"name":"Greenwald N."},{"name":"Kudo T."},{"name":"Moen E."},{"name":"Osterman E."},{"name":"Pao E."},{"name":"Schwartz M."},{"nam